A tremendously powerful (EXP21) wizard met a crushing end at the hands
of Orcus due to sheer stupidity. His goal was to bag an entire set of
named demons, and had already sacked Asmodeus, Geryon, Balzebub, and
Yeenoghu using expert Cone of Cold. And he aspired to sack the Big D.

It didn't happen; Orcus summoned Elbereth-ignoring nasties and
surrounded him. Since Lozr the Wizard was up past his bedtime at 3 AM,
he conveniently forgot that the Eye of Awesome could branchport him to
safety, and had no time to slip on an Amulet versus Typographical
Error.

Since I explored the entire game, sans the Sanctum and ascension run,
I feel obligated to comment on some salient aspects of Sporkhack:

1. Dragonbane is an amazingly useful artifact, because a weakling
character can use it to sack a dragon for DSM in a single hit. But
giving the character every resistance in the game seems too powerful
since (spoiler!) reflection no longer gives 100% physical protection.
A foodless, pacifist, or vegan character could manage a *much* easier
ascension with some good pets and a wielded dragonbane.

2. Ditto for Giantslayer, which now acts as Gauntlets of Power when
placed in your *alternate* weapon slot. It's almost unbalancing for an
elven wizard, who can wear gauntlets of dexterity or leather for the
spellcasting bonus while holding Giantslayer for boundless strength.

3. I think the new Gehennom is too easy, because the abundance of no-
teleport levels makes nasty-summoners with weak physical attacks such
as arch-liches almost powerless. Face it: if an arch-lich can't run
away and hog the stairs, he's basically toast, whether touch-of-death
lopes off HP or not. I think the caverns should have more monsters
inside, since reaching the downstairs is almost trivial with a
spellbook/wand of light.

The caverns and "slow" intrinsic, however, make jumping spells/boots
*much* more valuable during the late game, and make area-effect spells
such as Cone of Cold far more damaging than they already are.

4. Do named demons no longer respect Elbereth? Orcus certainly didn't;
he killed me even though I stood on an engraved E square. If Big D no
longer respects Elbereth, then... well, I guess I'll carry a
cockatrice egg in open inventory for my next trip to Gehennom. :)

5. The amulet of power is a very, very powerful addition and makes
wishing for the Eye rather than armor much less attractive. My early
wizard barely used his +6 dagger stack because magic missile + amulet
of power (polypiled using two amulets of restful sleep and an early
want of polymorph) is so powerful.

6. I *like* "ad aquarium". I always thought it silly that Croesus
would hide his gold in plain sight with such pitiful defenses.
However, the addition make gold-hunting easier! The eels won't attack
a pet, so my wizard could find the vault via telepathy, dig towards
it, and let his kitten tiptoe inside and retrieve the gold. Eels think
kittens are poor eating (read: low level) and will not attack them, so
this approach seems to be a surefire way to find and raid vaults.

In conclusion, I am certainly going to keep Sporkhacking, despite the
stupid connection error that lost his priest with -14 AC, GDSM,
Dragonbane, an amulet of power, and Giantslayer (Loser's last game:
Derek, could you recover this? I think it would be fun to run a priest
with an amulet of power!).



